  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Sunday)\n\nOne last mostly quiet day weather wise on tap, before an upper \ntrough prepares to move across the region. This also means one \nmore day of breezy winds for east-central Nevada, keeping fire \nweather conditions elevated to near critical as SW winds of 10 MPH\nto 20 MPH with gusts up to 35 MPH will possible for NE Nye, White\nPine, and SE Elko counties. Elsewhere winds will be lighter out \nof the SW at 5 to 15 MPH with gusts up to 25 MPH possible. Sunday \nnight and trough Monday, The GFS and ECMWF have continued to trend\na little bit farther south with the track of the trough, a bit \ndeeper, while continuing to depict a quick moving system. However,\njust as it exits Nevada, this trough will tap into tropical \nmoisture from Hurricanes Odalys and Polo, which will lead to a \nexcessive rainfall for Utah, Arizona, and points east. Depending \non timing there may be a window for wrap-around moisture to impact\nsoutheastern White Pine county Monday evening, but for now \nholding precipitation amounts steady as confidence is not quiet \nthere yet. That being said, there is a 20% to 50% chance for light\nisolated to scattered showers with a few thunderstorms \naccompanying trough passage late Sunday night through early \nTuesday morning. However the best chances at seeing rain has \ntrended south across central Nevada, with thunderstorm chances \nlimited to the southern portions of NE Nye, and White Pine \ncounties.. Amounts still look light with a trace to 0.05\u201d for \nnorthern Nevada, while central Nevada may see a trace up to 0.50\u201d \nfor the mountains of Great Basin National Park. Tuesday and \nWednesday shortwave ridging returns bringing another period of \nquiet weather conditions back to the Silver State. Thursday into \nnext weekend model agreement has been a bit better with recent \nruns, as models show ridging over the great basin, but there is \nstill a bit of disagreement on orientation of the upper flow as \nsolutions vary from NW to SW flow aloft. Temperature wise, a \ncooling trend is underway through Tuesday, with highs falling into\nthe mid 70s. Wednesday will start a new slow warming trend, with \nthe return of upper ridging as highs return to the lower 80s. Lows\nwill range in the mid to upper 40s for the first half of the \nforecast period, cooling into the mid to upper 30s by middle of \nnext week.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n \nThere is moderate to high confidence in the potential for a 20% \nchance for isolated showers across northern Nevada, and a 30% to \n60% chance for isolated to scattered showers and thunderstorms \nacross central Nevada Monday.\n\nThere is high confidence in the return of upper level ridging for\nthe middle of next week restoring quiet and dry pattern over \nNevada.",
